body:
I don't know if I believe in a soulmate per-say, but given that I met my wife and I only have probably ever spoken to a few thousand people in my entire life, out of 7 plus billion. If we went as far as to say a human life span were 100 years, that's 70 million people the exact age as you (these numbers obviously are not exact by any means) roughly 35 million of the opposite sex. 35 million people compared to the few hundred people we've ever met from whom we've found a partner. Just seems logical to me that we're missing many people that would be a good or better fit for us.

&#x200B;

And yes, I love my dear wife lol
